 "answer": "The default `keep_alive` value for the Ollama `/api/generate` request, as specified in the context from the project's documents, is set to `\"5m\"`. This means that by default, models are kept loaded in memory for 5 minutes after a request is made to the `/api/generate` endpoint. This setting helps in quicker response times for subsequent requests to the same model within that time frame.\n\nThis information is found in the section discussing the `keep_alive` parameter within the configuration for the Ollama provider:\n\n```yaml\nproviders:\n  - id: ollama:chat:llama3.2:3b\n    config:\n      num_predict: 1024\n      temperature: 0.7\n      top_p: 0.9\n      think: true # Enable thinking/reasoning (Ollama 0.34+ also accepts 'low'/'medium'/'high'/'max')\n      showThinking: true # Include the reasoning trace in the output (default: true)\n      keep_alive: '5m' # How long Ollama keeps the model loaded after the request\n```\n\nThis snippet indicates that the default duration for keeping a model loaded in memory after a request is 5 minutes.",
